      "message": "Are you sure `SUBTREE_MODIFIED` is ever actually delivered here? `AbstractRIBSupport.java:310-320` returns `route.childNodes()`, i.e. the individual route map-entries, and `EffectiveRibInWriter.writeRoute()` rewrites a route with a whole-entry tx.put(...) `EffectiveRibInWriter.java:484`, which resolves the entry to WRITE `SchemaAwareApplyOperation.java:216`.\n\nThe `SUBTREE_MODIFIED` you see belongs to the parent containers changedRoutes walks through. So for the target use case it looks like only the `WRITE` case fires.\n\nGiven that, would it be cleaner to keep the two as a single case SUBTREE_MODIFIED, WRITE -\u003e as before, and split on dataBefore inside it:\n```\n  if (route.dataBefore() \u003d\u003d null) {\n      entry.addRoute(routerId, pathId, (MapEntryNode) routeAfter);\n      totalPathsCounter.increment();\n  } else {\n      entry.updateRoute(routerId, pathId, (MapEntryNode) routeAfter);\n  }\n```  \nDoes that match the intent, or is there a delivery path where the entry really does arrive as SUBTREE_MODIFIED that I\u0027m missing?",
